<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_A-Subject_B_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_A-Subject_C_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_A-Subject_D_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_B-Subject_C_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_B-Subject_D_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.01706v1/Figures/FMRIs/Subject_C-Subject_D_Linear_Predictivity.png" id="A2.F2.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:176/146;" width="176" height="146" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure B.2: </span><span id="A2.F2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transport plans for linear predictivity-based mapping pairs.</span>
Pairwise mappings learned under linear predictivity constraints for all subject pairs:
(a) Subject A <math id="A2.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject B,
(b) Subject A <math id="A2.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject C,
(c) Subject A <math id="A2.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject D,
(d) Subject B <math id="A2.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject C,
(e) Subject B <math id="A2.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject D, and
(f) Subject C <math id="A2.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Subject D.
Unlike hierarchical OT, linear predictivity-based pairwise mappings do not recover structured layer-wise correspondences, highlighting the importance of hierarchical optimization for learning robust and generalizable mappings across subjects.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
